<!--/Post: 8678-->
<!--Post: 8680--><!--Time: 1109281530-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8680"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:witchkingofangmar@comcast.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 24, 2005 - 1:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ll just say W Harry between S Waco and S Main &#40;I simply cannot give up to many good hideouts---seriously, waiting near post boxes on anniversary dates, or by certain properties on anniversary dates is a favorite trick of mine&#41;...I figure if there is ONE trait he can&#39;t beak it&#39;s visiting sites important to him on anniversaries...Tuesday night was just a chance thing, one REALLY suspicious dude on a phone in his 50&#39;s-60&#39;s---too precious and wouldn&#39;t THAT be something. Some out of towner rolls into town not knowing anyone from Adam and gets WAY LUCKY, like the first time lottery ticket buyer who wins... <BR> <BR>Peace out for now...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8680-->
